   P=(5, 7, 11): gcd=1  off-lattice nonzero chat (n=1..300, tol 1e-7) = 0   max|chat| off = 0.00e+00   (on-lattice |chat| mass = 3.018)
   P=(2, 4, 6): gcd=2  off-lattice nonzero chat (n=1..300, tol 1e-7) = 0   max|chat| off = 6.77e-17   (on-lattice |chat| mass = 1.782)
   P=(3, 6, 9): gcd=3  off-lattice nonzero chat (n=1..300, tol 1e-7) = 0   max|chat| off = 1.94e-16   (on-lattice |chat| mass = 1.637)
   P=(2, 6): gcd=2  off-lattice nonzero chat (n=1..300, tol 1e-7) = 0   max|chat| off = 5.60e-17   (on-lattice |chat| mass = 1.566)
   => chat is EXACTLY supported on gcd(P)*Z: the Bohr/lattice support of HYP-2606.

